
# HG changeset patch
# User ndo84bw <ndo84bw@gmx.de>
# Date 1786270088 0
# Node ID 71a46731d0abcbe9c23476d92dbd376f3cd0ebd3
# Parent  d56b745fc12eebbc3b6314a943a945040064b960
Bug 1713625 - Clear the injected cache callback when the CalDAV calendar takes it, so an offline playback cannot run a previous operation's callback and delete the wrong event from the cache. r=darktrojan

`calCachedCalendar` hands the callback that updates its cache to the CalDAV calendar through the `_cachedModifyItemCallback` member, set immediately before it calls `modifyItem` on the uncached calendar. The callback was never cleared afterwards, so the next direct `modifyItem` call on the uncached calendar - in practice the playback of an offline modification - picked up the callback of the previous operation. That callback then paired the freshly played-back item with the previous operation's old item and wrote the pair into the cache: the previous event's row was deleted and the played-back event duplicated. Events silently vanish from the calendar until the cache is rebuilt, while the server stays correct the whole time. This is likely also the cause of bug 1694709 and bug 947138.

Take and clear the callback in one step in `adoptItem` and `modifyItem`. Remove the now redundant reset in `calCachedCalendar`, together with the `_injectedCallbacks` list that was never read.

`CalICSCalendar` receives the callbacks the same way and has the same problem; bug 2052714 fixes it there.

Add a test that modifies one event online and another one offline; without the fix, playing back the offline modification deletes the first event from the cache.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310485


